questions.question:
Before pasting logs into the assistant, a developer runs them through this function:

const redact = (text: string) =>
  text.replace(/(api[_-]?key|secret|token)\s*[:=]\s*\S+/gi, "$1=[REDACTED]");

The log being pasted:

10:41:07 POST /internal/leaderboard/refresh 500
  headers: { authorization: "Bearer FAKEopaqueAccessToken0123456789" }
  error: connect ECONNREFUSED postgres://codedev_app:Fake-Passw0rd!@db.codedev.test:5432/codedev
  config: { apiKey: "sk-codedev-FAKE-0000000000000000" }

Statement: "After redact(), the log can be pasted into the chat without exposing a credential."
